 game played by 2 players. You can play offline 2 players or play with Computer.  Initially 9 pebbles are given to both player. Aim is to create a Straight Line either Horizontally or Vertically. When a Straight line is created, you claim a pebble from Opposition that must not belongs to a Straight line.  When all pebbles are placed on desk, single movements starts. You will get 4 options \"Left\"/\"Right\"/\"Top\"/\"Bottom\" to move your pebble to create a Straight line.  When you claim all pebbles from opposition then you will win the game.  I added \"Online\" feature for simple conversation with online users. But for that, you have to login with your google account. Enjoy :-)","topics":["authentication","firebase","game"],"score":286059,"global_rank":29029},{"name":"sup/dotfiles","owner":"sup","html_url":"https://github.com/sup/dotfiles","stars":2,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Shell","description":":file_folder: Subset of dotfiles based off of https://github.com/mathiasbynens/dotfiles and some custom stuff","topics":[],"score":286044,"global_rank":29036},{"name":"codefellows/domain_modeling","owner":"codefellows","html_url":"https://github.com/codefellows/domain_modeling","stars":7,"forks":17,"watchers":42,"issues":0,"language":"Other","description":null,"topics":[],"score":286042,"global_rank":29038},{"name":"shanemhansen/gogeo","owner":"shanemhansen","html_url":"https://github.com/shanemhansen/gogeo","stars":8,"forks":2,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Go","description":"Go bindings to the GeoIP database","topics":[],"score":286033,"global_rank":29042},{"name":"ahelwer/quantum-experiments","owner":"ahelwer","html_url":"https://github.com/ahelwer/quantum-experiments","stars":3,"forks":3,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Q#","description":"Q# code snippets written when exploring quantum computing concepts","topics":[],"score":286033,"global_rank":29043},{"name":"rayz2007/GameReviews","owner":"rayz2007","html_url":"https://github.com/rayz2007/